The initial version of this Internet of Things project was developed
using simulated devices in Azure IoT Hub. This project collects air
quality data from the sensor and intersection data from cameras
in order to make AI based (scikit-learn, Random Forest) traffic
routing decisions. Azure IoT Hub was used for data collection and
message routing, while Azure IoT Explorer was used message
content visualisation. A QLearning Agent to make decisions on
sending traffic light commands from cloud to device. For
communicating with a web app MongoDB was used.
Later, the simulated devices were replaced with: Arduino with air
quality sensor and LED traffic lights, Raspberry Pi 5 (AI based
routing, communication with Jetson, Arduino and Azure), NVIDIA
Jetson Nano with Raspberry Pi v2 Cameras (C++ DeepStream AI
image processing for vehicle counting and traffic light state
detection). For low-level pixel processing C++ CUDA was used for
matrix and vector operations, taking advantage of the Jetson's full
capabilities. Data sets backups were also sent periodically (Linux
cron jobs) to Azure Blob Storage. End-to-end data flow, AI
accuracy, performance, reliability and multi user aspects about
this project are still in developement.
Simulated devices version:
https://github.com/ZavoiCalin/SmartTraffic525